 no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 36%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $66.01 to $113 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 27.1 vs 17.7 and EV/EBITDA 15.8 vs 10.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 16% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.5% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 6 covering analysts target $107 on average, 17% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 21% clears the cost of capital of 11.0% by 10pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 2.92).","It runs a 19% gross margin and converts 10% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.47x.","ROE of 13% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.4x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.8% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $614.5M (13% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 7.9, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.48)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.7% over 3 years, 13.4% over 5 years and 28.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 125%).","At current returns, reinvesting 12% of profits supports about 2.5% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 13.1% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.5% trend).","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (1.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 23, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.8%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $1.1M sold).","It returns 4.1% a year to shareholders (4.1% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 9,200 employees, each generates about $290K of revenue, 0.8x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 21.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $29K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":75,"head":"Watch: composite 54, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $72.36.","pros":["Composite 54, above the 39 line (gates 15/26)","ROIC 20.8% vs WACC 11.0%","FCF margin 10.1%","Revenue grew 13.4%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $614.5M"],"cons":["Trades 7% above fair value of $85.12","P/E 27.1x vs sector 17.7x","EV/EBITDA 15.8x vs sector 10.5x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":72.36,"vc":{"base":85.12,"base_src":"dcf","bear":66.01,"bull":112.86,"alt_median":53.17,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.862,"dispersion":0.3636,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (36% dispersion)","DCF is 86% above the other models' median ($53.17)"]},"med":{"pe":17.7245,"ev_ebitda":10.514,"pfcf":15.7535,"pb":2.1712,"roic":0.127,"gross_margin":0.3467,"fcf_margin":0.0625,"div_yield":0.0235}},"mc_quantiles":[53.46,61.61,66.01,69.17,72.2,74.35,76.5,78.86,80.92,83.01,85.3,88.07,90.51,92.35,95.11,98.49,102.9,106.32,112.86,121.75,142.27],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.707,"discount_rate":0.26,"terminal_growth":0.009,"exit_multiple":0.023},"ticker":"SKY","date":"2026-11-20"}